        "original_id": "dd867d4b-0c2d-5124-b66d-75e99ac2d56e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kuk Harrell, Rihanna, Beyoncé, Diane Warren, Ryan Tedder, Brent Kutzle, Britney Spears, Michael Jackson, Christina Aguilera, Katy Perry, Gwen Stefani\n- Songs: \"Only Girl (In the World)\", \"Umbrella\", \"I Was Here\"\n- Albums: \"Loud\"\n- Groups: Destinee & Paris\n- Places: New Jersey, Los Angeles\n- Concepts: vocal production, songwriting, musical influences, Grammy Awards, Billboard No. 1 singles\n\nFacts:\n- Rihanna recorded \"Only Girl (In the World)\" for her fifth album \"Loud\" in 2010.\n- Kuk Harrell earned his fourth Grammy for the vocal production of Rihanna's Billboard No. 1 single \"Only Girl (In the World)\".\n- Kuk Harrell was also the vocal producer and co-writer of Rihanna's Grammy-winning single \"Umbrella\".\n- Diane Warren wrote the song \"I Was Here\".\n- Ryan Tedder, Brent Kutzle, and Kuk Harrell produced \"I Was Here\", and Beyoncé received vocal production credit on the song.\n- Destinee & Paris are sisters who were born and raised in New Jersey and later became based in Los Angeles.\n- Destinee & Paris have cited Britney Spears, Michael Jackson, Christina Aguilera, Beyoncé, Katy Perry, Rihanna, and Gwen Stefani as musical influences.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
